  "chain": "cable erroneously labeled spare [cause A] -> cable cut during unrelated modification (2022-03) -> breaker close signal not delivered on DG run relay pickup -> Unit 1 West MDAFP fails to auto-restart during DG 1AB load sequencing -> AFW train inoperable ~17 months, exceeding TS 3.7.5 AOT [manual start capability retained; East MDAFP/TDAFP available, no Loss of Safety Function]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Discovery occurred during DG 1AB load sequencing test in U1C32 refueling outage; past operability review extended the inoperability window back to May 19, 2022 (previous outage U1C31 Mode 3 entry). Manual start from control room remained available throughout, but this is an operator-action mitigation, not a distinct System/backup node per the narrative's framing (no separate ECCS/backup system named as operable substitute for the train itself). RCE was in progress at time of report; cause code A (Personnel Error) is provisional per licensee pending RCE, but FORM-366 cause_code is not 'TBD' so provisional flag left false per rule 4. No previous similar events per licensee 3-year review."
}